 "content": [
  {
   "children": [
    "working-paper, architecture, framework"
   ],
   "tag": "aside"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A working paper written on 2026-11-16, published nearly as written. Local file paths, private repository names and personal names have been removed."
   ],
   "tag": "blockquote"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Status:"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " code, 2026-10-17. Linear ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NA-24"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ", with NA-270 (treatment) and NA-276 (NPCA offset). Synthetic tests only in git."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "How a City of Hamilton parcel (and its addresses and buildings) gets a permanent Industrial Atlas ID. The ID format is ADR 0003. The spine grammar is parcel-identity-spine.md. Findings that drove the rules are SPINE-BASE-PULL-2026-10-17.md and quirks Q-001–Q-019."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Nothing here is published. Pulled rows stay in local data (not published). Owner and other identifying field ",
    {
     "children": [
      "names"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " may appear in config denylists; values are dropped on load and never written to the registry."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "What-gets-minted"
   },
   "children": [
    "What gets minted"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "parcel"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Spine key: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "ia:ca:on:hamilton:parcel:{ULID}"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " · Source: City Assessment Parcel polygons · Collapse rule: one ID per distinct geometry; ",
      {
       "children": [
        "OBJECTID"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      "s become aliases"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "address"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Spine key: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "ia:ca:on:hamilton:address:{ULID}"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " · Source: City Addresses · Collapse rule: one ID per ",
      {
       "children": [
        "number|street|community|unit"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      "; several points share it"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "footprint"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Spine key: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "ia:ca:on:hamilton:footprint:{ULID}"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " · Source: City Buildings · Collapse rule: one ID per distinct footprint; overlap list kept"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "ARN is ",
    {
     "children": [
      "not"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " minted. It is attached to a parcel ID with a grade."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Matching-aids-(never-the-ID)"
   },
   "children": [
    "Matching aids (never the ID)"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "geom_hash"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — SHA-256 prefix of rounded, rotation-normalised rings. Detects the 83 stacked City duplicates (Q-001) and exact re-pulls."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "fingerprint"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — ",
      {
       "children": [
        "{rep_x:.2f}:{rep_y:.2f}:{area:.2f}"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " in EPSG:26917. Second-chance re-pull key."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "ARN"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — 15-digit roll number from NPCA Assessment_Parcels_Test, after the Q-004 shift."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Geometric-correction"
   },
   "children": [
    "Geometric correction"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Per-source translation, applied ",
    {
     "children": [
      "before"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " matching, in the working CRS (EPSG:26917):"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "City parcels, addresses, buildings"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — dx_m: 0 · dy_m: 0"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "npca_assessment_parcels_test"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — dx_m: +0.297 · dy_m: −0.939"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "npca_parcels_cityview"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        },
        " (same hosted offset; Owner field not used)"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — dx_m: +0.297 · dy_m: −0.939"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "City fabric is the reference (PI-0013). Inputs must already be in EPSG:26917. Lon/lat GeoJSON is refused so the metre shift cannot be applied to degrees."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "ARN-grades"
   },
   "children": [
    "ARN grades"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Assigned to each City parcel when an NPCA layer is supplied. Reciprocal representative-point containment, then rolled up by ARN."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "exact_1to1"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: this parcel and this ARN point at each other only"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "one_to_many"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: this ARN also attaches to other City parcels (City grain is finer)"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "many_to_one"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: this City parcel holds more than one ARN"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "placeholder"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: the attached value is a documented sentinel (all-zero ARN). It is recorded, not grouped with real ARNs, and not shown as a roll number"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "unmatched"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: inside or within 5 m of NPCA coverage, no attachment"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "not_in_coverage"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: farther than 5 m from any NPCA polygon (~46% of the city)"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Placeholder detection runs ",
    {
     "children": [
      "before"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " grouping by ARN (PI-0059). All-zero values used to grade ",
    {
     "children": [
      "one_to_many"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " because the sentinel repeats. They now grade ",
    {
     "children": [
      "placeholder"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " and feed ledger type ",
    {
     "children": [
      "placeholder"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " (data-gaps-ledger.md). A non-Hamilton prefix with real digits (Grimsby ",
    {
     "children": [
      "2615…"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", Q-019) stays ",
    {
     "children": [
      "non_city_prefix"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " and is not a placeholder. Re-running the registry does not change existing ",
    {
     "children": [
      "ia_id"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " values: placeholders change the ARN grade, not identity."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "These are registry attachment grades. They are not the NA-86 ",
    {
     "children": [
      "exact"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " / ",
    {
     "children": [
      "good"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " / ",
    {
     "children": [
      "weak"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " / ",
    {
     "children": [
      "refused"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " scale (still open)."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Parcels_Cityview is a secondary, stale ARN source. This code path does not load it by default, and it will not copy ",
    {
     "children": [
      "Owner"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " or ",
    {
     "children": [
      "Legal_Txt"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " if someone passes that file."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Addresses-and-buildings"
   },
   "children": [
    "Addresses and buildings"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Address → parcel: point-in-polygon. If the point is in no parcel, nearest parcel within 10 m. If it is in two distinct parcels, ",
      {
       "children": [
        "pip_ambiguous"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " and no link (stacked duplicates have already collapsed)."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Building → parcel: largest intersection area. The full overlap list is stored. Waste Collection by Address is an optional unit-coverage cross-check (",
      {
       "children": [
        "waste_seen"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " = ",
      {
       "children": [
        "y"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      "/",
      {
       "children": [
        "n"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      "), not an ID source."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Re-pull"
   },
   "children": [
    "Re-pull"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Match active registry rows by ",
      {
       "children": [
        "geom_hash"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", then by ",
      {
       "children": [
        "fingerprint"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", then by unique IoU ≥ 0.9. Those keep their ID."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Remaining one-old-to-many-new with overlap: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "split"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — new IDs, ",
      {
       "children": [
        "split_into"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " lineage, parent retired."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Remaining many-old-to-one-new: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "merge"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — new ID, ",
      {
       "children": [
        "merged_from"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " lineage, parents retired."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Remaining 1:1 below 0.9 IoU: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "replaced_by"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — new ID, parent retired."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Remaining new shapes mint new IDs. Remaining old rows retire. Retired locals stay in the issued set."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ol"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Address IDs persist by civic key. Building IDs use the same polygon reconcile rule at footprint grain."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Persistence"
   },
   "children": [
    "Persistence"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
